DRMRAW(1)                      ZOAU Command Syntax                     DRMRAW(1)

NAME

	drmraw - Remove one or more VSAM cluster or non-VSAM datasets.

SYNOPSIS
	drmraw [-dfhv] [<dataset>]+

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-f
		If the dataset does not exist, do not issue a message.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-v
		Issue a message for each deleted dataset.

DESCRIPTION

	drmraw removes the specified VSAM clusters or non-VSAM datasets.
	No wildcards are expected in dataset names. Use the drm command
	to work with dataset patterns.

EXAMPLES

	Delete the dataset IBMUSER.PROJ22.JCL and the dataset IBMUSER.PROJ23.JCL

		drmraw 'ibmuser.proj22.jcl' 'ibmuser.proj23.jcl'

	Delete datasets TESTER01.PROJ23.TEXT and TESTER02.PROJ23.JCL.
	Print a message for each dataset deleted. If the datasets do not exist,
	do not print an error message

		drmraw -vf tester01.proj23.text tester02.proj23.jcl

EXIT VALUES

	0
		drmraw completed without error.

	1
		Dataset specified by dataset pattern does not exist.

	non-zero
		Errors occurred. See error messages for details.

SEE ALSO
	drm(1), rm(1), dls(1)
